WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Chemists loved CFCs.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:07.680
They were non-toxic, they would not burn,
and they barely reacted with anything.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.900
They filled fridges and spray cans,

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.840
and for decades they slowly
drifted up into the sky.

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.840
High above, a layer of ozone absorbs
harmful ultraviolet radiation.

6
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:25.140
In 1985, scientists reported a large
springtime loss of ozone over Antarctica.

7
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.120
So how can a little gas
destroy so much ozone?

8
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.220
In this mission, you'll see
how ozone shields the Earth,

9
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.040
and what happens to CFCs
high in the atmosphere.

10
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.420
Then you'll follow the evidence
that got CFCs phased out,

11
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.340
and meet the gases that replaced them.

12
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.070
Your mission: explain how a little
gas can destroy so much ozone.